  "_note_expect": "expect filled from the driver's completed run on the final tree (control 0); no two mutants share a red set (checked by tuple(sorted(expect))). M1+M4 together are the origin/main behaviour (raw-label fallback, no block disambiguation) — the base flip as mutants, since the new exports do not exist on origin/main and the suite would fail structurally there (§A83). M17/M28 are the review-round-1 HIGH (re-resolving already patched rows rebuilds the whole-vault index on every metadataCache change): L20 counts getMarkdownFiles calls across 20 change events on a fully patched block. M4 and M29 share an anchor on purpose — the driver applies each mutant to the untouched source. The `text === null` term of the tier-3 guard carries no own mutant: dropping it breaks type-narrowing (string|null into Map<string,string>), i.e. BROKEN, not behavioural (§A36); M7/L4 pin its behaviour."
